  "title": "CHAPTER 1: CONSTITUTIONAL PROVISIONS FOR HINDI AND OFFICIAL LANGUAGE",
  "order": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b3awm8x",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Hindi as Official Language :Constitutional Basis"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 343(1) designates Hindi in Devanagari script as the Official Language of the Union.",
        "Part XVII of the Indian Constitution contains the constitutional provisions regarding the Official Language from Articles 343 to 351.",
        "The Eighth Schedule of the Indian Constitution lists 22 Scheduled Languages.",
        "Article 351 places a constitutional duty on the Union to promote the spread and development of the Hindi language."
      ],
      "id": "k3nocmp"
    },
