    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Article 343 specifically establishes Hindi in Devanagari script as the official language of the Union of India.",
        "Questions frequently ask about the exact count of languages listed under the Eighth Schedule, which stands at 22.",
        "Article 351 is often tested as the constitutional directive for the promotion and development of Hindi."
